{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Investigation complete — two independent defects, not one\n\nRead-only investigation finished. Every conclusion below is backed by a reproduction; nothing is inferred.\n\n### Defect 1 — landed on `origin/main`: default path is outside the sandbox\n\n`Makefile:239-246` on `origin/main`:\n\n```make\n\t@set -e; \\\n\ttarget_dir=\"$(if $(dir),$(dir),../$(name))\"; \\\n```\n\nFrom a clone at `~/rebar`, `../$(name)` resolves under `~/`, outside the repository working directory, which the agent filesystem sandbox refuses. Verified directly:\n\n```\n$ mkdir ../sandbox-origin-main-67033\nmkdir: ../sandbox-origin-main-67033: Operation not permitted\n```\n\nand end to end through the real target:\n\n```\nfatal: could not create leading directories of '../sandbox-origin-dry/.git': Operation not permitted\n```\n\n### Defect 2 — unpushed local commit `7b92d821718`: a make comment inside a continued shell recipe\n\nThis is the source of the `/bin/sh: branch: No such file or directory` failure, which is NOT a consequence of the path problem. Local `Makefile:239-245`:\n\n```make\n\t@set -e; \\\n\t@# Default is ~/worktrees/rebar/<branch>, NOT a sibling of the checkout.\n```\n\n`@set -e; \\` continues the same shell command, so the following line is not a make comment — the shell receives it as a command. `#` is not a comment character inside the word `@#`, so `<branch>` parses as an input redirection from a file named `branch`. The shell fails opening it before command lookup ever happens. Minimal reproduction confirms the mechanism:\n\n```\n+ @# Default is /Users/joeoakhart/worktrees/rebar/ NOT a sibling of the checkout.\n/bin/sh: line 1: branch: No such file or directory\n```\n\nA scan found exactly one backslash-continued recipe line followed by an `@#` line, so no other target shares this defect.\n\n### Status of `7b92d821718`\n\nIt changes only `Makefile`, moving the default from `../<branch>` to `~/worktrees/rebar/<branch>`. It **partially** addresses defect 1 and **introduces** defect 2, so `make worktree` is currently broken outright rather than merely mis-targeted.\n\nIt is local-only and was never reviewed. `origin/main` does not contain it (`exit=1` on the contains check), and Gerrit queries by commit, by subject, and by this ticket id all returned empty. Its own commit message states it was committed directly to local `main` without a Change-Id, without a `rebar-ticket` trailer, and without going through Gerrit.\n\n**Operator action needed:** that commit sits on the shared checkout's `main` and actively breaks the target. It is not mine to discard — mutating the shared checkout is forbidden by project guidance because it may hold operator work in progress. Flagging it for a human decision.\n\n### Chosen destination, and why\n\n`~/worktrees/rebar/<branch>` was tested and *is* writable on this host — so the premise of `7b92d821718` is not wrong here. It is still rejected, because it depends on a grant outside the working directory that other agent sandboxes need not provide.\n\nThe recommended default is `.rebar/worktrees/<branch>`, verified on three counts:\n\n```\n$ mkdir -p .rebar/worktrees/sandbox-candidate-67927   -> exit 0\n$ git worktree add .rebar/worktrees/probe -b probe HEAD -> exit 0\n$ git status --short --ignored .rebar/worktrees/probe -> !! .rebar/worktrees/\n```\n\n`.gitignore:24` already ignores `.rebar/*`, so the path is inside the sandbox-writable working directory, works for real worktree creation, and cannot pollute tracked content or appear as untracked work.\n\n### Test coverage gap\n\n`tests/unit/test_makefile_worktree.py` exercises the target but always passes an explicit `dir=`, so it bypasses default-path selection entirely. `tests/unit/test_worktree_python_pin.py` only asserts recipe contents. **No existing test asserts the default target path, and none would have caught either defect.**\n\n### Unresolved\n\nAuthenticated Gerrit state could not be checked — `git credential fill` returned no Gerrit HTTP credential in that session. Public queries returned nothing, so the conclusion that the commit was never sent for review rests on the public view plus the commit message's own statement.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789669208130409787,"uuid":"46a8767c-0c76-47d0-b71e-2a8e560ee369"}